.\n\nAttestation schema:\n{:edge {:from :pattern-id\n        :to :pattern-id\n        :kind #{:why :how :see-also}}\n :by :agent-id\n :at :date\n :read [:pattern-id]\n :cited :nonblank-string\n :evidence [{:id :evidence-id\n             :via #{:tag :text}\n             :query :nonblank-string\n             :excerpt :nonblank-string}]\n :rung #{1 2}\n :state #{:proposed [:attested-by :agent-id] :refused}\n :reason :optional-nonblank-string}\n\nSection README:\n(No section README exists.)\nSection pattern ids:\n[\"aif/admissibility\" \"aif/belief-aware-risk-term\" \"aif/belief-state-operational-hypotheses\" \"aif/candidate-pattern-action-space\" \"aif/currency-before-merge\" \"aif/declare-the-conditioning\" \"aif/decomposed-prediction-noise\" \"aif/evidence-precision-registry\" \"aif/expected-free-energy-scorecard\" \"aif/experimental-comparison-of-EFE-variants\" \"aif/free-energy-as-tick-scalar\" \"aif/grounded-actuation-not-reobservation\" \"aif/hierarchical-budget-aware-action-selection\" \"aif/measurement-window-hygiene\" \"aif/niche-construction\" \"aif/no-self-certification\" \"aif/off-continuity-null-discriminates\" \"aif/placeholder-is-load-bearing\" \"aif/policy-precision-commitment-temperature\" \"aif/posterior-variance-as-epistemic-value\" \"aif/predictive-coding-belief-update\" \"aif/predictive-entropy-as-ambiguity\" \"aif/scheduled-observer-entrypoint\" \"aif/shared-kernel-predictive-forward-model\" \"aif/status-gated-belief-update\" \"aif/structure-learning-by-model-reduction\" \"aif/structured-observation-vector\" \"aif/temporal-depth-beyond-greedy\" \"aif/term-to-channel-traceability\" \"aif/two-layer-calibration\" \"aif/valuation-reads-the-paperwork\"]\n\nSelected pattern text:\n@flexiarg aif/niche-construction\n@title Niche Construction as the Bootstrap Loop of an Inference Agent\n@sigils [🐜/巢]\n@keywords niche-construction, bootstrap, typed-edge-inventory, false-floor, substrate, generative-model, anamnesis, mana, agency, action-class, ΔT\n@audience operators of fulab / futon-stack agents, mission authors, designers of read/write substrates for an active-inference engine\n@references [aif/expected-free-energy-scorecard aif/structured-observation-vector futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation]\n@references-extra [\"Lewontin (1983) on niche construction in biology\" \"Odling-Smee, Laland, Feldman (2003) Niche Construction: The Neglected Process in Evolution\" \"Friston (2010, 2017) on active inference and policy selection over external structure\" \"Andy Clark (1997, 2008) on scaffolded cognition and extended mind\" \"Mission of origin: ~/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-action-cost-modelling.md §3.8 + §5.1 T9 closure (2026-05-27 emacs-repl, claude-1 + Joe)\" \"Constant, Ramstead, Veissière, Friston et al. — A variational approach to niche construction (variational free-energy applied to niche construction)\" \"Kiverstein & Miller (2023) — Playfulness and the meaningful life: an active inference perspective (PMC10656941)\"]\n@tone declarative\n@style pattern\n\n! conclusion: An inference agent whose generative model depends on an externally-authored substrate cannot, *as currently architected*, construct its own niche; the agents operating its peripherals do, and the agent's false-floor readings are how those agents know what to construct. (Scope matters: this is a property of the current niche-authoring arrangement, not a theorem about active inference — see HOWEVER-endogenous below.)\n\n  + context: An active-inference agent (e.g. the futon War Machine) reads a substrate of typed vertices and edges, computes T / ∇T / ΔT or analogues, and ranks actions. Its inference is bounded by the typed-edge inventory of the substrate it can see. The substrate is itself authored by other agents and operators.\n\n  + IF:\n    You are designing an AIF agent whose generative model depends on a structured substrate (hypergraph, knowledge graph, typed event log) that is authored by parties other than the agent itself.\n\n  + HOWEVER:\n    The agent cannot extend its own substrate's typed-edge inventory — it has operations on values within the niche but not on the meta-level structure of the niche. When action classes surface that the inventory doesn't cover, the agent reads ΔT = 0 (false floor), not error. It looks confident-and-wrong; it is in fact correctly-uninformed, and the substrate is incomplete.\n\n  + THEN:\n    Treat false-floor readings as **niche-construction signals**, not bugs. Each false-floor names a typed-edge family the substrate is missing relative to the action classes agents actually take. The operators-and-agents who use the inference agent do the niche construction: they add the missing typed-edge families, ingest the missing vertex types, derive the missing relations. On the next tick the agent sees a richer niche and ranks more accurately.\n\n  + BECAUSE:\n    Niche construction (Lewontin 1983; Odling-Smee / Laland / Feldman 2003; Friston in active-inference terms) is the loop by which an organism modifies its environment so its inference becomes tractable. The futon agent is in the same loop; only the niche is symbolic (a typed graph) rather than physical. Confident false-floors masquerading as signal is the worst outcome — the agent makes apparently-warranted-but-actually-uninformed choices. Visible false-floors that operators can read as \"edges missing here\" is the right outcome — the agent's blindness becomes the input to its own niche's improvement.\n\n  + HOWEVER-endogenous (2026-05-31, claude-1 + Joe, emacs-repl):\n    The \"cannot\" above is scoped to the current architecture, where the substrate is authored by parties other than the agent. It is NOT a theorem about active inference. Two strands show the boundary can be redrawn so niche-construction becomes endogenous: (a) hierarchical AIF learns high-level priors that re-weight uncertainty-tolerance — Kiverstein & Miller (2023) on playfulness: a learned high-level prior expands the phenotypic bound on tolerated surprise, sending the agent to the competence edge where new structure is found; (b) the variational free-energy principle has been applied to niche construction directly (Constant / Ramstead / Veissière / Friston, \"A variational approach to niche construction\"), redrawing the Markov blanket to include the constructed niche so inventory-edits become variational moves over an extended boundary rather than an external handoff. The futon realisation is the **aif2** direction: a boundary-tier set of criteria (mechanising AIF+ I1 boundary-integrity + I3 timescale-separation) over whether and how the WM may re-author its own typed-edge support — distinct from the inference-tier R1-R12. The false-floor / zero-anamnesis lull, under a learned playfulness prior, reads not as \"hand off\" but as \"forage at the edge\" — the niche-construction trigger from the inside. See M-aif2.\n\n  + NEXT-STEPS:\n    - Surface false-floor readings as such — don't silently zero-out a signal; report \"ΔT = 0 (no incident edges of supported family)\" so absence is legible to operators.\n    - When new action classes are added to a ranking surface, audit which typed-edge families would feed ΔT (or analogue) for that class, and which are present-vs-missing in the substrate.\n    - For the futon stack as of 2026-05-27: the WM's ΔT over `code/v05/related-mission` works for sorry-actions but gives ΔT = 0 false-floor for anchor-reframe / file-edit / excursion-step actions. Construction backlog: (a) feed `code/v05/mission-cross-ref` (already in substrate from M-weird-modernism Task 8 single-parser consolidation) into the Laplacian; (b) derive `code/v05/file → mission` from `:mission/code-paths`; (c) ingest E-prefix excursion docs as a typed vertex family (currently not ingested).\n    - Connection to aliveness synthesis (M-action-cost-modelling §3.8): anamnesis = un-discharged tension drives niche construction; niche construction discharges anamnesis into mana. The three terms form a single loop, with niche construction as the operative mechanism by which agent-substrate aliveness shifts.\n    - Sibling-pattern dependency: when authoring missions that ship new action classes, the mission's INSTANTIATE phase should explicitly enumerate the niche-construction-audit per class (which edges feed the Laplacian, which are absent). Treat per-class niche-construction state as first-class mission metadata, not implicit.\n    - aif2 / endogenous niche-construction (2026-05-31): treat the action-class inventory itself as hidden state to be inferred (an extension of R12, or candidate R13), and mechanise the AIF+ I1 (boundary integrity) + I3 (timescale) invariants for the case where the boundary is *permitted to move*. The meta-model is `futon2.aif.*` modelled as its own AIF+ `.aif.edn` lifeform. See M-aif2 (IDENTIFY).\n",
